<title>NETHERLANDS: KLM shareholders to meet on share buy-back.</title>
<headline>KLM shareholders to meet on share buy-back.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Flag carrier KLM Royal Dutch Airlines said on Friday it would hold an extraordinary meeting of shareholders on March 3.</p>
<p>&quot;In this meeting, the KLM shareholders will be asked for permission to buy back and cancel ordinary KLM shares,&quot; the company said in a statement.</p>
<p>Last December, KLM said it would buy back 17.29 million of its own shares from the Dutch state. This will cut the state's interest in the airline to 25 percent from 38 percent.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
